{"input_text": "Question: I have a problem to calculate
At the given picture the line segments AB , AC , FE ,GH , GI are known
I want to calculate the line segment ED
Is this posible ?
Thanks in advance
Nikos 

Answer: According to the intercept theorem, it follows that:
$$
\begin{align}
\frac{ED - BC}{HI - BC}=\frac{FE - AB}{GH - AB}
\end{align}
$$ 
 To solve for $ED$, you would get: 
 $$
\begin{align}
ED =\frac{(FE - AB)(HI - BC)}{GH - AB} + BC
\end{align}
$$ 
 I hope this helps.. 
