{"input_text": "Question: I have given matrix with me as follows . I need to calculate $A^{50}$ . Hint is to diagonaize it ,but since it has repeated eigen values so can't be diagonalized.Can any1 help me with this  
 $$A=\left[\matrix{ 1 & 1 & 1 \\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\ 0 & 0 & 1 }\right]$$ 

Answer: Instead of diagonalization, one can compute $A^{50}$ using the fact $A$ is upper triangular and hence its off-diagonal part $B = A - I$ is nilpotent. i.e 
 $$B^3 = (A-I)^3 = 0$$
This implies 
 $$A^{50} = (I + B)^{50} = I + \binom{50}{1} B + \binom{50}{2} B^2 + 0 + \ldots\\
= \begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1\end{bmatrix}
+ 50 \begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 1\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\ 0 & 0 & 0\end{bmatrix}
+ 1225 \begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 0\end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix}1 & 50 & 1275\\ 0 & 1 & 50 \\ 0 & 0 & 1\end{bmatrix}
$$ 
